Package: iomdisparity
Type: Package
Title: Implementing the Institute of Medicine Healthcare Disparity Definition
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Kaes", "Holkeboer", email = "kaesholk@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
  )
Description: Implements the Institute of Medicine (IOM) definition of racial and
    ethnic healthcare disparities using the rank-and-replace algorithm developed
    by McGuire et al. (2006) <doi:10.1111/j.1475-6773.2006.00583.x>, Cook et al.
    (2010) <doi:10.1111/j.1475-6773.2010.01100.x>, and Cook, McGuire, & Zaslavsky
    (2012) <doi:10.1111/j.1475-6773.2012.01387.x>. Provides tools for calculating
    need-based health indices, quantile mapping, single-part GLMs, two-part
    expenditure models, stratified bootstrap confidence intervals, multi-method
    reporting (unadjusted, residual direct effect, and IOM rank-and-replace),
    and counterfactual distribution visualizations.
